':'''
"""kora - one VM at a time, local or cloud.

Manages exactly one virtual machine per state home (KORA_HOME). Local VMs run
under tart (macOS guests + Linux guests on Apple Silicon), QEMU+hvf (Arch
aarch64 on macOS, via the archboot unattended installer) or QEMU+KVM (official
cloud images + cloud-init on Linux hosts). Cloud VMs are QEMU+KVM guests on a
persistent clouddevbox named 'kvm' (one per AWS profile); kora installs itself
on the box and proxies verbs there, so the box-side state is the single source
of truth - running kora on the box shows the same machine.

Stdlib-only: the external dependencies are binaries (tart, qemu-system-*,
ssh/scp, genisoimage/mkisofs/xorriso, clouddevbox), never pip packages.
"""
